meta {
  name: Fail mode - set
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

put {
  url: {{stubHost}}/emp-stub/fail-mode
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "mode": "update"
  }
}

docs {
  none | add | update | all.

  Set "update" and re-run request 03: updateResults comes back with
  success: false and an error description, which is an API-level failure rather
  than the connection error you would get from an unreachable host. The backend
  handles those two differently, and this is the one its retry and dead-letter
  path actually exercises.

  Set back to "none" when finished, or the next transition will fail too.

  An unknown mode returns 400 and leaves the current mode alone.
}
